{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level","id":1518051,"title":"What is the Malkavian Anatole actual generation level?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-15T10:16:11-07:00","id":1518051,"title":"What is the Malkavian Anatole actual generation level?","content":"I'm thinking of possibly placing Anatole in my character's lineage and I'm unclear is he a member of the 8th generation and which case would make him a great grand-sire or is he a member of the 7th generation like his mates Beckett and Luciata are or is even lower as there is stories of him committing amarath on numerous Kindred in the past. The lore seems to contradict what is generation is on wikepedia and Google.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T11:07:12-07:00","id":1518057,"title":"","content":"His sire was Pierre l'Imbecile according Clanbook: Malkavian (Revised Edition) p.99 and Transylvania Chronicles 3: Ill Omens p.74, he was originally a 10th Generation Vampire<br /> Pierre l'Imbecile was and still is a a 9th Generation Malkavian (actice, or at least not reported to be dead) as per Transylvania Chronicles 3 and Transylvania by Night<br /> Sadly we don't know who Embraced Pierre, we only know he Embraced Anatole in 1193 in Paris where Anatole born 1173 under a blue moon, and he was a a pious vampire.<br /> As for Anatole, in Transylvania Chronicles IV: The Dragon Ascendant, on p. 88, on his character sheet he was stated as 6th Generation after in Transylvania Chronicles 3: Ill Omens he commited Diablerie<br /> He became the Voice of Kupala after - as per Transylvania by Night, p. 79-80 - a 6th generation Malkavian, the previous Voice of Kupala allowed Anatole to diablerize him, making Anatole keeper of the mysteries and the harbinger of Gehenna, and passed him to mantle<br /> Octavio himself was originally 7th Generation, Embraced by a Roman Malkavian, Marcus, but Octavio's ties to the dark soil or the Carpathians forced him to commit several vile acts, culminating in the staking and diablerie of his sire, becoming 6th<br /> So it is 100% certain Anatole was a 10th Generation Malkavian and eded up as a 6th Generation one where he currently is<br /> He had a Child tho, an unnamed one, Anatole mentioned that he had lost a childe to the Chosen of Calomena (Chosen of Calomena was a cult of clanless Caitiff in medieval Constantinople, that sought to the destroy vampires. Led by Stanislav, they were originally from the Balkans and were seen as mad prophets. They thought themselves the champions of the fabled Calomena, the sister of Caine. - they were mentioned in Constantinople by Night)<br /> <br /> So the Line is Malkav (3) - ? (4) - ? (5) - ? (6) - ? (7) - ? (8) - Pierre l'Imbecile (9) - Anatole (originally 10, now 6 after the Diableire of Octavio)<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-15-2023, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T11:25:25-07:00","id":1518060,"title":"","content":"Well may the Forum sensitive spam filter be damned and burn in one of the Hells of Yomi<br /> Okay, again<br /> <br /> His sire was Pierre l'Imbecile according Clanbook: Malkavian (Revised Edition) p.99 and Transylvania Chronicles 3: Ill Omens p.74, he was originally a 10th Generation Vampire<br /> Pierre l'Imbecile was and still is a a 9th Generation Malkavian (actice, or at least not reported to be dead) as per Transylvania Chronicles 3 and Transylvania by Night<br /> Sadly we don't know who Embraced Pierre, we only know he Embraced Anatole in 1193 in Paris where Anatole born 1173 under a blue moon, and he was a a pious vampire.<br /> As for Anatole, in Transylvania Chronicles IV: The Dragon Ascendant, on p. 88, on his character sheet he was stated as 6th Generation after in Transylvania Chronicles 3: Ill Omens he commited Diablerie<br /> He became the Voice of Kupala after - as per Transylvania by Night, p. 79-80 - a 6th generation Malkavian, the previous Voice of Kupala allowed Anatole to diablerize him, making Anatole keeper of the mysteries and the harbinger of Gehenna, and passed him to mantle<br /> Octavio himself was originally 7th Generation, Embraced by a Roman Malkavian, Marcus, but Octavio's ties to the dark soil or the Carpathians forced him to commit several vile acts, culminating in the staking and diablerie of his sire, becoming 6th<br /> So it is 100% certain Anatole was a 10th Generation Malkavian and eded up as a 6th Generation one where he currently is<br /> He had a Child tho, an unnamed one, Anatole mentioned that he had lost a childe to the Chosen of Calomena (zhe Chosen of Calomena was a cult of clanless Caitiff in medieval Constantinople, that sought to the destroy vampires. Led by Stanislav, they were originally from the Balkans and were seen as mad prophets. They thought themselves the champions of the fabled Calomena, the sister of Caine. - they were mentioned in Constantinople by Night)<br /> <br /> So the Line is Malkav (3) - ? (4) - ? (5) - ? (6) - ? (7) - ? (8) - Pierre l'Imbecile (9) - Anatole (originally 10, now 6 after the Diableire of Octavio)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T12:43:38-07:00","id":1518064,"title":"","content":"Thanks Shadeprowler about the info and maybe it would be better if I kept Anatole out of my character's lineage all together and maybe just make up my own kindred line and come up with my own 4th generation methusalth that my 11th generation ancilla descended from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:06:32-07:00","id":1518068,"title":"","content":"There is three &quot;canon&quot; lines we know of:<br /> <br /> Malkav (3) - Lamdiel (4) (CbR-M) - Addemar (5) (CbR-M) [Embraced in 500 BC, Death in 1887 CE] - Trimeggian (6) (CbR-M) - Dr. Douglas Netchurch (7) (CbR-M) [Embraced in 1880] - Dr. Nancy Reage (8) (CbR-M, Time of Thin Blood, Ghouls: Fatal Addiction) [Embraced in 2000]<br /> <br /> Malkav (3) - Brahina (4) (Transylvania Chronicles II) - Unmada (5) (CbR-M, Transylvania Chronicles II) [Embraced in 369] - Vasantasena (6) (CbR-M, Transylvania Chronicles II) [Embraced in 1000]<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Malkav (3) - Panehesy (4) (Lair of the Hidden) - Pashedu of Thebes\u200b (5) (Lair of the Hidden) - Demetrius of Antioch (and his alternate identity, the Master of Ravens) (6) [Embraced in 320]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:15:05-07:00","id":1518070,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of using Necrosiss from Vancouver as one of my characters ancenstor as they both share a desire for learning dark secrets and lore. I had some notion of using Emmlich from Children Of The Night, but I'm thinking of going with my own home brewed 4th generation childe of Malkav myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T14:09:59-07:00","id":1518082,"title":"","content":"Anatole's a compulsive diablerist, so any individual childe of his could theoretically be anywhere from 11th to 7th generation. He was embraced 10th and ate his way up to 6th. It's also important to note, this would be an exception to the &quot;age loosely correlates to generation&quot; rule -- younger childer of his would be <i>lower</i> generation thanks to elder vampires' tendency to trip and fall into his tummy. So basically any generation at which a PC could start works for a vampire of Anatole's lineage, especially given Malkavians' tendency toward broken lineages making the matter easier to adjudicate.<br /> <br /> He's also a Dominate Malkavian, so any of his lineage would be likely to have their discipline spread adjusted accordingly. Not a big deal in v5 if that's what you're playing, as Dementation was rolled into Dominate as amalgam powers, but still.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T14:13:12-07:00","id":1518083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1518070#post1518070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of using Necrosiss from Vancouver as one of my characters ancenstor as they both share a desire for learning dark secrets and lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Necross happens to be one NPC i'm using in my current chronicle where, in a sort of bizarre way to connect the Great Library in Vancouver with the Library of the Forgotten from Constantinople by Night, i made it so Necross is either <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gregorius_Dimities\" target=\"_blank\">Gregorius Dimities</a> after consuming <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Keeper_of_the_Faith\" target=\"_blank\">Keeper of the Faith</a>, or perhaps the opposite, a doubt that is something of a stumbling block of sorts in the mad plans of my group's version of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vukodlak\" target=\"_blank\">Vukodlak</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1518070#post1518070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had some notion of using Emmlich from Children Of The Night, but I'm thinking of going with my own home brewed 4th generation childe of Malkav myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Elimelech\" target=\"_blank\">Elimelech</a> and.... yeah, that is one NPC who can be all kinds of sketchy to bring to one's table and make sense of. Making some extended lineage of one's own will probably be safer and more engaging, imho.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> And speaking of elusive 4th gen Malkavians, one might also consider the sire of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cybele\" target=\"_blank\">Cybele</a> and grandsire of Olympias/<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Petaniqua\" target=\"_blank\">Petaniqua, </a>as the Shaitan of Cnossos being NOT Nergal as the Baali &quot;clanbook&quot; claims but a Malkavian ancient even in the time of Thera's destruction gone Apostate/Forsworn would go a long way towards solving issues over their lineages, among other continuity issues.\u200b<br /> <br /> (If that makes him one and the same as OG Shaitan / Huitzilopochtli from Chaos Factor or someone else altogether, that would be up to you as ST to decide).\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> But back on the main subject, it's exactly as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> pointed out - Anatole by canon is very much of a serial diablerist, meaning any individual childe of his could hypotetically be anywhere from 11th to 7th generation depending on the time of embrace and in fact childer embraced in closer to modern* times should be much more potent than any earlier ones from the middle ages.<br /> <br /> <br /> *For a <b><i>very</i></b> loose definition of &quot;modern&quot; since, according to the Wiki, Anatole would reach 6th generation through the consumption of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Octavio\" target=\"_blank\">Octavio</a> sometime in the early 1700s. Meaning even his &quot;latest brood&quot; could include individuals already considered as ancillae or elders in their own right. That's about century over Lodin, Modius or a number of canon princes in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T13:35:02-07:00","id":1518152,"title":"","content":"You think I would used to the ever changing generation levels for Kindred and take into account that amaranth is fairly normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T16:04:32-07:00","id":1518158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1518064#post1518064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Shadeprowler about the info and maybe it would be better if I kept Anatole out of my character's lineage all together and maybe just make up my own kindred line and come up with my own 4th generation methusalth that my 11th generation ancilla descended from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what are you aiming for in cobbling together an extended lineage for that Malkavian? How much of that impacts on the backstory of whatever city one's chronicle is set into, are there any bits of lore or metaplot from any books or games you'd like to weave some elusive link toward for your character? Just messing around with making a little bit of crypto-lore of your own?<br /> <br /> Lineages can be slippery things, so much so that the Clan Novels had something of a recurring theme of....<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Victoria_Ash#Trivia\" target=\"_blank\">canon characters</a> getting their precise generations wrong, for a funny example.<br /> So no problem with having confusing, undetailed or sketchy bits on one's lineage, most kindred don't keep precise track, glossing over obscure ancestors (and diablerie instances) to proclaim themselves of better pedigree than they really are.<br /> <br /> ....unless you are the potent childe of some infamous monster that decides to do the opposite, because you have learned that being underestimated is safer (specially when being a neonate of potent blood can make you into a prime target of diablerists of varied generations), that is.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T17:11:22-07:00","id":1518159,"title":"","content":"At Baaldam. Right now it\u2019s only in the initial stages and it\u2019s more of a creative exercise at this point and I\u2019m thinking that my Malkavian\u2019s grand and great grand sire being his mentors as Mithras decided to spare my character\u2019s and put his sire to final death for not asking permission to do it.<br /> <br /> Why I don\u2019t know yet and I\u2019m leaning towards that even the Ventrue doesn\u2019t know either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T20:16:56-07:00","id":1518163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1518159#post1518159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Baaldam. Right now it\u2019s only in the initial stages and it\u2019s more of a creative exercise at this point and I\u2019m thinking that my Malkavian\u2019s grand and great grand sire being his mentors as Mithras decided to spare my character\u2019s and put his sire to final death for not asking permission to do it.<br /> <br /> Why I don\u2019t know yet and I\u2019m leaning towards that even the Ventrue doesn\u2019t know either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras, so i'm guessing probably London (though it doesn't have to be so - Mithras left the city under Valerius's stead for a good chunk of the 19th century for reasons unstated - my current pet theory is that after the american debacle he got in the mood to tackle <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Anglo-Indian_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">colonization from the forefront</a>, and might have had a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Veddartha\" target=\"_blank\">personal</a> interest in the Danava at least) and sometime up to WW2, since he disappeared again sometime during the Blitz and from that point onward <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anne_Bowesley\" target=\"_blank\">Lady Anne</a> is the one who would rule the city up to the present.<br /> <br /> About reasons, who knows - princes can do things for a number of reasons incredibly arcane or utterly mundane.<br /> It's kind of a coin toss if the motive has anything to do with acts of one's ancestors or anything else altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T09:51:00-07:00","id":1518176,"title":"","content":"I might have to change it to Valerius being the Prince of London if I want to be accurate to the time line lore as the ancient blood god would have been in topor by the time my character was born and embraced and Mithras wouldn't show up until the mid 1880's and by then my Malkavian would've been only a Kindred for a few scant decades and slowly thinking of moving to the New World for better opertunities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-17-2023, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T08:51:18-07:00","id":1519113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1518176#post1518176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have to change it to Valerius being the Prince of London if I want to be accurate to the time line lore as the ancient blood god would have been in topor by the time my character was born and embraced and Mithras wouldn't show up until the mid 1880's and by then my Malkavian would've been only a Kindred for a few scant decades and slowly thinking of moving to the New World for better opertunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, is that Malkavian a NPC you are fleshing for a chronicle or a PC you intend to play in someone else's table? Depending on the case you can have differing degrees of freedom to take liberties with canon &amp; continuity according to your preferences.<br /> <br /> But if you want some canon, there's some <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517850-fall-of-london-feedback?p=1519108#post1519108\">London-related</a> tidbits across books both obvious and not. That said, there's nothing stopping you from getting NPCs or plot threads from wherever you want. Anatole and Lucita aren't in no way british, nor is Bindusara - and yet he was obviously there for some reason in 1066, since he not only witnessed the Battle of Hastings but would embrace his childe Valerius at it, for example.<br /> <br /> Nothing stopping your Malkavian of having commited some secret off-screen Amaranth on the side either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Canon is only as big a deal as one wants to make of it.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T09:44:22-07:00","id":1519115,"title":"","content":"My Malkavian is my main player character at this point as I've decided to give my Brujah ancilla a well deserved holiday Baaldam. As for Amaranth that is something that my character wouldn't be considering at this point in his &quot;life&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T16:40:22-07:00","id":1519133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1518068#post1518068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is three &quot;canon&quot; lines we know of:<br /> <br /> Malkav (3) - Brahina (4) (Transylvania Chronicles II) - Unmada (5) (CbR-M, Transylvania Chronicles II) [Embraced in 369] - Vasantasena (6) (CbR-M, Transylvania Chronicles II) [Embraced in 1000]</div> </div> </div> </div>Little nitpick - Unmada diablerized a Tzimisce right before embracing Vasantasena, it's right there in her original write-up in Children of the Inquisition.<br /> That said, i suspect very, very few kindred would know of that little detail or have many ways to check (or dare to).<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1518176#post1518176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have to change it to Valerius being the Prince of London if I want to be accurate to the time line lore as the ancient blood god would have been in topor by the time my character was born and embraced and Mithras wouldn't show up until the mid 1880's and by then my Malkavian would've been only a Kindred for a few scant decades and slowly thinking of moving to the New World for better opertunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let's summarize things a bit:<br /> - 11th Malkavian generation ancilla.<br /> <br /> - embraced during the 1800s in London, without permission to do it. His sire was put to final death for doing so, but the Prince (or seneschal) decided to spare the character\u2019s unlife*.<br /> <br /> - since he &quot;would've been a Kindred for a few decades and slowly thinking of moving to the New World** for better opportunities&quot; by the mid 1880's when Mithras reappears, i'm guessing his embrace would more precisely have been sometime in the middle of XIX century (1840s-1860s?), during Valerius' extended stewardship of the city.<br /> <br /> - the Malkavian's grand and/or great grand sire assume the role as his mentor(s)***, educating him to properly fit into kindred society.<br /> <br /> - has a desire for learning dark secrets and lore, much like Necross from DA: Vancouver (possible ancestor? unseen guide through the Cobweb? both, neither? who knows)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *That reminds somewhat of the begining of VtM: Bloodlines. What do you think of doing a &quot;Victorian Bloodlines&quot; backstoryline for your Malkavian, with Valerius as Lacroix's expy, trying to yank his chain and gain power to usurp Mithras by diablerizing some methuselah in a smuggled sarcophagus, Abraham Mellon or Edward Bainbridge in place of Strauss and chinese vampires (or setites) infiltrating the city? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> **Anywhere in particular in mind? Any special reason for going to the Americas instead of, for example, the Near East, British India (that included what today is Pakistan and a bunch of other places), Australia or a number of other places under the aegis of british colonialism? (Or who knows, maybe he did for some time...)<br /> <br /> <br /> ***One, both or did they take turns at instructing him? Who and how are they, gender, personality, manias or peculiar powers &amp; traits? Does the PC know or remember much of anything about its destroyed sire, for that matter.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Just my two cents of thought and ramblings of the moment. Hope it's helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-29-2023, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T10:28:01-07:00","id":1519181,"title":"","content":"I appreciate any useful feedback and suggestions to improve my gameplay or amalgam power ideas Baaldam. I enjoy the creative aspects of trying to make a decent character in any game and I have the start of the \u201cfamily\u201d tree starting with basic concept for his 4th generation founder and how some his actions started a slow progression to my player character motivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-30-2023, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T13:10:14-07:00","id":1519196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1519181#post1519181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate any useful feedback and suggestions to improve my gameplay or amalgam power ideas Baaldam. I enjoy the creative aspects of trying to make a decent character in any game and I have the start of the \u201cfamily\u201d tree starting with basic concept for his 4th generation founder and how some his actions started a slow progression to my player character motivation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's all a matter of what you are looking for.<br /> <br /> In what city (in the Americas i suppose) this Malkavian exists in contemporary times (Also, what counts as &quot;contemporary&quot; in a table, for that matter - 2020s, 2010s, 2000s, the 90s or 80s)?<br /> - Where does he stand in the local food chain? Depending on a city's age, that of its kindred and atrition of the local Jyhad, a 140+ years ancilla could be anything from barely noticed domain-holder or hound to even primogen or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lodin\" target=\"_blank\">prince</a>. All up for grabs depending on the city one picks and how much lore there is or not about it.<br /> <br /> Defining when in the 19th century was he born and embraced should be relevant too, since <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/19th-century_London\" target=\"_blank\">the city</a> of London can vary considerably depending <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_London_(1800s)\" target=\"_blank\">on decade</a> (what is also one of my main peeves with London by Night, in that their definition of &quot;victorian age&quot; only covers a very narrow span of the 19th century and even then not that well).<br /> <br /> What derangement(s) does the Malkavian have? How aware and connected (or not) to the Cobweb/Madness Network it is?<br /> <br /> Does he have childer? In London, his current home city, both, neither? How many? Is he still in contact with his mentor(s)?<br /> <br /> You mentioned an interest in dark secrets and lore - Do you mean dark secrets as in obscure bits of lore like 'the Salubri might have created the Baali&quot; or the Cappadocian Feast of Folly, or would that also involve finding the dark secrets of kindred he currently interacts with, digging the dirt in one's local court, possible hidden players and such?<br /> <br /> <br /> Look for something to pique your interest and develop/improvise from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-02-2025, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T01:25:14-07:00","id":1519229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1519133#post1519133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Little nitpick - Unmada diablerized a Tzimisce right before embracing Vasantasena, it's right there in her original write-up in Children of the Inquisition.<br /> That said, i suspect very, very few kindred would know of that little detail or have many ways to check (or dare to).<br /> \u200b<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but eating that chamberlain not lowered her generation<br /> Brahina was his sire in 4th century and the only &quot;sure&quot; thing we know about her is that she was the childe of Malkav <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T04:44:34-07:00","id":1519238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518051-what-is-the-malkavian-anatole-actual-generation-level?p=1519229#post1519229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but eating that chamberlain not lowered her generation<br /> Brahina was his sire in 4th century and the only &quot;sure&quot; thing we know about her is that she was the childe of Malkav <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, quite debatable to honest. Plus, remember &quot;childe of Malkav&quot; can <b>also </b>be a moniker to anyone of the clan, instead of a reference to being a literal 4th generation. <i>Caveat Emptor.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T09:21:19-07:00","id":1519445,"title":"","content":"Thanks Baaldam for some the pointers for what I should also consider for my player character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}